From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 09:35:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] driver core: demote fw_devlink sync-state link failures

Upstream-Status: Pending [needs review for generic fw_devlink users]

fw_devlink can create inferred SYNC_STATE_ONLY links to keep supplier
sync_state() callbacks ordered with consumers that may appear later. These
links do not enforce probe ordering or runtime PM dependencies.

On AM335x tiny boot, always-on timer target modules can trigger inferred
SYNC_STATE_ONLY attempts against the OCP ancestor. If such a link cannot be
created, device_link_add() returns NULL and the driver core currently emits a
dev_err(), even though the attempted link only affects sync_state() behavior.

Demote failures for SYNC_STATE_ONLY links to dev_dbg() while preserving the
existing dev_err() for real device-link failures.

Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/base/core.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -2120,7 +2120,12 @@ static int fw_devlink_create_devlink(struct device *con,
 		}
 
 		if (con != sup_dev && !device_link_add(con, sup_dev, flags)) {
-			dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with %s\n",
+			if (flags & DL_FLAG_SYNC_STATE_ONLY)
+				dev_dbg(con,
+					"Skipped sync-state-only device link (0x%x) with %s\n",
+					flags, dev_name(sup_dev));
+			else
+				dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with %s\n",
 				flags, dev_name(sup_dev));
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 		}
